From ec0c931e5be140ecfc29d94503d750b6c3e68239 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 11:59:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] doc/examples/encode_audio: set the timestamps of the frames

The frames were sent to the encoder with pts left at AV_NOPTS_VALUE, so
the packets it returned carried no timestamps either. That goes
unnoticed here because the packets are written out raw, but code derived
from this example and feeding a muxer would write a stream without
timestamps.

Set pts to the number of samples sent so far, in the default audio
encoder time base of 1 / sample_rate.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FZ4G6798n6Ua4qu6xwWu3S
---
 doc/examples/encode_audio.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/doc/examples/encode_audio.c b/doc/examples/encode_audio.c
index e9ede0d..a22d645 100644
--- a/doc/examples/encode_audio.c
+++ b/doc/examples/encode_audio.c
@@ -249,6 +249,9 @@ int main(int argc, char **argv)
                 samples[c->ch_layout.nb_channels*j + k] = samples[c->ch_layout.nb_channels*j];
             t += tincr;
         }
+        /* the timestamp is in time_base units, which defaults to
+         * 1 / sample_rate for audio encoders */
+        frame->pts = (int64_t)i * c->frame_size;
         encode(c, frame, pkt, f);
     }
 
